{"t": 1794111439.7771428, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "## Red `main` pipeline \u2014 root cause and fix\n\n**Failure:** pipeline 8812 (`main`, a91c2e0), job `test:contract` (77104).\n\n```\ncontract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format\n    assert invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"\nE   AssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\n**Root cause:** `billing/invoice.py` formatted the number with a bare sequence (`f\"INV-{year}-{seq}\"`), so the sequence was not padded. The ERP v2 import contract (FIN-77) requires the sequence part to be zero-padded to 6 digits; the contract test already encodes that requirement, so `main` has been red since a91c2e0.\n\n**Fix:** format the sequence as a 6-digit zero-padded field:\n\n```python\ndef invoice_number(year: int, seq: int) -> str:\n    return f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\n**Verification (local, same assertion as the contract test):**\n- `invoice_number(2026, 42)` -> `INV-2026-000042`\n- `invoice_number(2026, 0)` -> `INV-2026-000000`\n- `invoice_number(2025, 123456)` -> `INV-2025-123456` (already 6 digits, unchanged)\n\nWith this change `test:contract` passes and the `main` pipeline goes green. No other jobs were failing (`lint` passed).", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
